        "heading": "1. they used to laugh with their hearts...",
        "text": "they used to laugh with their hearts and laugh with their eyes: but now they only laugh with their teeth, while their ice-block-cold eyes search behind my shadow.\n\nThere was a time indeed they used to shake hands with their hearts: but that's gone, son.\n\nNow they shake hands without hearts while their left hands search my empty pockets.\n\n'Feel at Home!' 'Come again\": they say, and when I come again and feel at home, once, twice,\n\nthere will be no thrice- for then I find doors shut on me.",
