   "theory": "Glossary\n\nReading Comprehension\n\n1. What is the main theme of the story 'The Last Leaf '?\n\n2. How did Sue and Johnsy become friends?\n\n3. \"She has a chance if she wants to live. If people don't want to live, I can't do much for them.\" What do these words of the doctor about Johnsy mean?\n\n4. Why did Johnsy keep asking Sue to open the curtains?\n\n5. How was Johnsy's life saved?\n\n6. What made Johnsy's views change about life? How do you know it?\n\n7. Write a short character sketch of the character Behrman in the story 'The Last Leaf '.\n\n8. Describe the plot of this short story in your own words.\n\n9. What lesson do we get from the story 'The Last Leaf '?\n\n10. Suggest an alternate ending for \" The Last Leaf\".\n\nWriting Suggestions\n\nWrite a summary of the story 'The Last Leaf ' using the technique of proper beginning, middle and end.\n\nOral Communication\n\nTake turns standing each student of the class. Ask them to say 3—4 compliments about his/her desk fellow using good and positive words. The use of negative words/ comments may strictly be prohibited.",
