   "theory": "Reading Comprehension\n\n1. Why did the cosmologists need a telescope in space well above the Earth's atmosphere?\n\n2. What does the author mean by the sentence \"when we look at stars we look at history\"?\n\n3. Why will the life on,Earth not disturb even if our galaxy Milkyway colloids with its neighbouring Andromeda?\n\n4. What is the Hubble Deep Field?\n\n5. How does the formation of stars take place in star nurseries?\n\n6. How do scientists study the atmosphere of an exoplanet through \"fingerprint\" technique?\n\n7. How will you explain in astronomical terms the statement, \"what you see is not always what you get\"?\n\nWriting Suggestions\n\nA. Comparison and Contrast Essays\n\nA compare and contrast essay looks at the similarities and differences between two or more objects.\n\nMethods for Organization: Compare and contrast essays are structured in two main ways.\n\n1. Block Structure\n\nFor the block structure, all information about one object being compared/contrasted is given first, and information about the other object is listed afterwards.",
