   "content": "<p>Reading Comprehension</p><p>1. What is the theme of the poem &#x27;The Toys&#x27;?</p><p>2. The story behind the poem &quot;The Toys&quot; is a homely one. Narrate the story in your own words.</p><p>3. What verse style has been adopted by the poet in the poem,&#x27; The toys &#x27;?</p><p>4. Does this style suit the mood of the poem and how?</p><p>5. What is the symbolic significance of the word &quot;Toys&quot; in light of the poem &#x27;The Toys&#x27;?</p><p>6. How does the poet relate his own action to the mercy of God?</p><p>7. What is the tone of the poem &quot;The Toys&quot;? Do you think it is in conformity with the theme of the poem? How?</p><p>8. What feelings does the poem &quot;The Toys&quot; evoke in you?</p><p>Writing Suggestions</p><p>Paraphrase the following lines:</p><p>&quot;Then, fatherly not less</p><p>Than I whom Thou hast moulded from the clay,</p><p>Thou&#x27;lt leave Thy wrath and say,</p><p>&#x27;I will be sorry for their childishness&#x27;.</p><p>Oral Communication</p><p>Give oral recount in front of class of your experience, feelings emotions if you had been treated by one of your parents the same way as narrated in poem &#x27;Toys&#x27;.</p><p>Vocabulary and Grammar</p><p>A. Fill in the following blanks with appropriate words related to weather given in the list below.</p><p>1. It&#x27;s very ________ today. I think it&#x27;s a northern wind.</p><p>2. They got married on a ________, sunny day in June.</p><p>3. Wait till the weather is ________ to take a bike ride.</p><p>4. Some people prefer to hike when it&#x27;s ________ rather than when it&#x27;s sunny.</p><p>5. I hate ________, cold days when I can&#x27;t warm up.</p><p>6. The weather is rather ________ today. You should take a rain jacket.</p><p>7. Next week will be hot and ________.</p><p>8. The weather is ________ this week. I wish it would rain.</p>",
