     "text": "At the age of 17, Jahangir Khan, astounded the world by beating the World number one Geoff Hunt of Australia in the final to become the youngest champion of The World Open in 1989. This tremendous victory proved to be the scratch line for the journey of his success that went on as unstoppable as the wind for five hundred and fifty five matches consecutively in the next five years (1981-1986). It is the longest winning streak by any athlete in the top level professional sports as per the record of Guinness Book of World Records. During his distinguished career, he won The World Open Championship for six times and the British Open , a record ten times in a row from 1982 to 1991.",
