   "content": "<p>Reading Comprehension</p><p>1. Why do we need more technical education than general education in Pakistan?</p><p>2. How did technical education help Japan and Germany recover their economy after World War II?</p><p>3. Why is a linkage between the industries and the technical education training centres necessary?</p><p>4. What measures do you suggest for improving the technical education structure of Pakistan?</p><p>5. How can technical education help in strengthening the economy of Pakistan?</p><p>Writing Suggestions</p><p>Write an argumentative essay on &#x27;Need for Technical Education in Our Country&#x27; by stating and opinion about the topic and list ideas that sport opinion.</p><p>Oral Communication</p><p>Pakistan needs skilled manpower through technical education for development, while everyone here wants to become an officer by getting general education. This trend must change. Make groups and Discuss.</p><p>Vocabulary and Grammar</p><p>A. Following are some words related to economics. Place each word in the given blanks that best define this word.</p><p>1. client, customer</p><p>A ________ is someone who buys goods or services. A ________ receives professional services.</p><p>2. career, job</p><p>A ________ is what someone does in exchange for money. A ________ is a professional trajectory that includes both past and present jobs.</p><p>3. coworkers, colleagues</p><p>A ________ is someone who works on your team or for your company. A ________ is a professional who works in your industry, but not necessarily for the same company</p><p>4. top-of-the-line, expensive, premium, overpriced</p><p>________ simply means that something costs a lot. ________ means that something costs more than it should. ________ and ________ have a positive connotation and communicate that something is high quality.</p><p>5. ordinary, standard, run-of-the-mill, , familiar, well-known, common</p><p>________ and ________ have a neutral connotation. ________ and ________ have more of a negative connotation. ________ and ________ have a positive connotation.</p><p>6. rich, well-off, well-to-do, wealthy</p><p>________ is direct term that we often try to avoid. ________ is a more polite way to communicate that someone has a lot of money. ________ and ________ are euphemistic, indirect ways to communicate that someone has a lot of money.</p><p>7. approach, method, Strategy, scheme, , plot,</p><p>________ and ________ have a negative connotation. ________ and ________ sound more positive.</p>",
