   "content": "<p>Reading Comprehension</p><p>1. What is the narrator&#x27;s job and the purpose of his journey? What physical conditions persuade him to rest for a few hours?</p><p>2. About how old is Cheng-Yu? What does he respond when the narrator asks,&quot;Why isn&#x27;t anybody home?&quot;</p><p>3. What work do Cheng-Yu&#x27;s parents do?</p><p>4. What &quot;job&quot; has Cheng-Yu been assigned.</p><p>5. What explanation does Cheng-Yu give for refusing the narrator&#x27;s advice to go to sleep?</p><p>6. What does the narrator do in the final paragraph? What does he realize is waiting for him?</p><p>7. What sort of child is Cheng-Yu? What attitude does he display towards his parents and his responsibilities?</p><p>8. What change in mood or outlook does the narrator experience in the course of the story? What causes the change?</p><p>9. What ideas about work does the story convey? What else does the story suggest is valuable?</p><p>Writing Suggestions</p><p>Write the story of the lesson &quot; Lingkuan Gorge &quot; with proper beginning, middle and end.</p>",
