   "content": "<p>Reading Comprehension</p><p>Answer the following questions</p><p>1. What is the world&#x27;s view of tourism potential in Pakistan?</p><p>2. What are the natural attractions for the tourists in Pakistan?</p><p>3. What is the historical importance of &#x27;Karakoram Highway&#x27;?</p><p>4. Which religious sites attract the tourists to Pakistan? What is their significance?</p><p>5. How is Baluchistan important for tourism?</p><p>6. How can we improve the global image of Pakistan to attract tourists from around the world?</p><p>7. Highlight Pakistan as a tourist destination for &#x27;Buddhist&#x27; and &#x27;Sikh&#x27; tourists.</p><p>Writing Suggestions</p><p>Write a description of a visit you made to somewhere that interests you. It may be a visit to an archaeological site, a museum, a zoo or a healthy mountainous area. The essay should start with a clear introductory paragraph with a central thought. Provide key ideas which prove, explain or support the central thought. Use a separate paragraph for each key idea.</p><p>Oral Communication</p><p>Each student should write three statements about themselves on a piece of paper. Two of them should be true, and one should be false. Students read their three statements, and their classmates question them to try to determine which statement is false.</p>",
