   "theory": "In a game, the boys pretend Robert is the hunted animal and get carried away. Ralph turns them back to the purpose: climb the mountain and relight the fire. After a hard journey along the shore, tired, Ralph decides to return to the platform and climb the next day.\n\nJack challenges him by setting off up the mountain at once, and the others follow, so Ralph must go too. Jack goes ahead and comes back shaken: he saw something “bulge” on the top and heard a “plop”.\n\nFor the first time Ralph senses Jack hesitate, and leads Jack and Roger up in the dark. On the summit they see a hump like a great ape sitting with its head between its knees; the wind stirs and it lifts “the ruin of a face” towards them. The three flee in terror, leaving the mountain to the bowing thing.",
